WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.401
-I don't know how to sit.

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.571
-You did a great job.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.239
You always overthink it.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.640
Did you overthink
sitting right now?

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.041
-Well, you know,
like when you're,

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.143
I don't know, filming anything
and they're like,

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.877
talk on the phone,
but make it look natural

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.013
and then you don't because
you're overthinking it.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.782
-Yeah
-I just overthought sitting.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.216
-Yeah.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:18.852
You look pretty good sitting.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.919
-It looks like
you've done it before.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.654
-I watched.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.123
-You've researched a lot
of tape and stuff and stuff.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:25.591
-Lot of years of sitting.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.861
-You're one of the best sitters
I've ever sat next to.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.629
-I appreciate that.
-You're welcome, yeah.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.464
-This is your talk show debut.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.166
-Yes, sir. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.001
-I'm honored.
I'm honored that you're here.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.236
-It's an honor to be here.
-Welcome.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.905
-Yeah, first of many times.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.007
You're in one of the biggest
shows in the world right now.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.342
"The Night Agent."

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.610
People can't
stop talking about this,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.945
but there's another role
that you played

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.646
that people can't stop
talking about.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:48.948
And if you know
what I'm talking about,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:52.819
But you were once
on the show "iCarly."

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.420
-Yeah.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.922
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.390
-Is that you?
-That is me.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.491
-Yeah.
-It's hard to tell.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.859
-Yeah, yeah.
-I think the whole premise

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.193
of the show
is it was hard to tell.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:03.663
Yeah. What was it, like,
a bizarro world or what was it?

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.064
Like, You played Freddy.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.533
-So I had my own idea
of what should have happened

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:12.604
where there's like a battle
for who gets to be Freddy,

00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:15.407
you know, and the fakes
try to remove the real ones.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:17.010
But they didn't like that.
It's Nickelodeon.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.845
-Yeah, I know.
Of course, yeah.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:22.148
What do you remember
about doing it?

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.950
-I don't remember much,
to be honest.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.985
I forgot that this happened
until recently,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.420
and everyone was reminding
me of it.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.788
-Because the Internet
just loves it.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.657
-Yeah. So I don't remember.
-You don't remember?

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.159
-It was fun, I guess,
as a kid.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.595
-Yeah. And now it's having
a resurgence.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.530
-Yeah.
-How long have you been acting?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.899
Since how old?
How young were you?

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.868
-13 to 18,
and then I quit

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.536
for like seven or eight years.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.204
-And you quit
because you just go

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.605
it's -- I don't feel like it,

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:47.907
it's not for me
right now or...?

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.875
-I just...

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:53.445
I think actors are really
insulated from reality.

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:54.780
And I think of all people,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.049
actors should be the least
insulated people

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.119
because they got to, like,
portray real things.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:04.257
And so everything sort of felt
like a pseudo experience to me,

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.992
like, as a kid where,
oh, you can be the fighter

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:09.628
And then not actually
hit anybody

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:11.364
or know what it's like
to get hit or whatever.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.898
It just felt very fake.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:15.067
So I quit because I was --

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.235
I didn't want to be depressed.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.871
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.340
-Good, good.
Good luck, buddy.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.908
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:22.908
-And now I'm back.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:24.977
-Yeah, now you're back.
Yeah.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.413
You got a smile on your face.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.648
-Yeah.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.883
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.853
-But you can do so many things.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.956
I was looking on the Internet

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.958
about the different skills
that you --

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.226
-I hope it was on
the Internet,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.061
and you're weren't,
like, watching.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.563
-I wanted -- Yeah, I'm --
I'm watching every move.

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:47.734
Yeah, but you can
you're -- you're skilled

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.936
at knife throwing,
archery, weightlifting,

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.805
professional fighting, drums...

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.873
-Amateur fighting, yeah.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.174
-Yeah. Sorry.
I aided professional.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.042
-I don't get paid.

00:02:57.042 --> 00:03:01.547
-Drums, violin,
drawing, welding.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.083
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.653
It's fantastic.
-I don't have a social life.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:07.753
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.355
-Yeah, no.
But, I mean,

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.925
this is one of the other
things you just, I guess...

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.361
Did you just get a Master?
What do you get?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.629
-Oh. So, yeah.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.365
I got my DSWA
walling license,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.566
so that's dry stone.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.368
I'm a stonemason.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.904
-So, you know, how --
how did you...

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.006
-So I have a trade.
I'm useful.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.274
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.542
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.444
Yes, you are useful.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.612
Yes.
-Yes.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.046
-You are useful.

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:35.414
But this is beautiful.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.283
This is --
I'm so jealous of this.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.352
I couldn't do anything
like this.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.387
I couldn't do.
That's a gorgeous wall.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:44.757
And when someone builds someone
a wall, it better be good

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.825
because it has to stand
the test of time.

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:47.893
-Yeah, I hope it does.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:49.328
And that's sort of
the funny thing

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.363
is you're building
these things that, I don't know,

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:53.733
kind of put this business
in context because you're like

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.903
this will last way longer
than people --

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.404
than my show will last.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.805
And then you go outside

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:01.441
and you're looking
at your wall...

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.509
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:07.479
It's not really funny.
It's just sort of like --

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:09.648
-I think, again, you're being
a little hard on yourself.

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.016
-I think it's a good thing

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:15.621
because I think people
have so much ego about stuff

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.523
and to look at a wall
and be like,

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:22.028
wow, if they lost their Wi-Fi,
they couldn't watch my show.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.230
But this wall, like,
serves a purpose

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.864
and will be around.

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:27.099
It just...

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.567
[ Laughs ]

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.768
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.737
Dude, you're...

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:34.573
You have to come back
on the show.

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.542
You're one of my favorite
guests we've ever had.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.445
You're fascinating to me.
I agree with you.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:42.114
That wall will last for...

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:45.151
-It should.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.586
-I don't know.
-No, I --

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:49.855
I think you got something.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:50.990
Let's talk about
"The Night Agent,"

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.625
because this is --
it already got picked up

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:55.027
for another season.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:56.028
-We're still on one.
-Well done.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.730
-Thank you.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.198
Thank you.
-How does it feel?

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:02.434
Because I know you do the show,
you work hard on it,

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.604
and then it comes out and then
everyone's watching and you go,

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.673
"Oh, this is kind of cool.
People are talking about this.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:10.176
I didn't know who would, like,
if it would catch on

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.944
or be as big as..."
It's giant.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:15.681
-It's always nice
when people enjoy things,

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.816
but especially
when it's like your art.

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:20.552
But for me,
it's a little uncomfortable

00:05:20.552 --> 00:05:22.054
because I do pen
and ink illustrations

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.123
and stuff and, like,
that's me.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.225
That's from my head.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:29.462
This is so, like,
collaborative.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:32.764
And when you're done
and you're working, you're done.

00:05:32.764 --> 00:05:35.601
And then everything that happens
that everyone else sees

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.070
was so out of your control
and out of your hands

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.540
that it's sort of like people
compliment you

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.042
because society sees it's you,
but then you're like,

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:46.545
but I didn't edit
the stuff.

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:50.450
I didn't -- I didn't do anything
other than my job.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:55.154
So it's, like, it's just
uncomfortable for me.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:57.857
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.257
Like --
-This is the realest interview

00:05:59.257 --> 00:06:00.659
I've ever had in my life.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.995
It's unbelievable, fascinating.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:07.033
-I remember I had
a camera operator.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.201
-Just keep going.
Keep going.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:11.937
-There was a camera operator
buddy of mine.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.906
-Tell me about it.
-And I just...

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.575
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:18.210
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.878
-I think this is --
-I have a good --

00:06:19.878 --> 00:06:22.014
I have a good fix for you.
-You do?

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.416
-Yeah, let me
fix you real quick.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.117
-You have a -- you have
a good fix for me.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.553
But -- so you have...

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:29.922
-So, -I'm looking at the camera
operator and I'm like,

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:33.058
wow, this job does not happen
without a camera operator.

00:06:33.058 --> 00:06:35.394
And in the same way, it doesn't
happen without a focus puller.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:39.031
So it's like we're all
sort of working together,

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.899
and then the end product
though,

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:42.501
everybody's like, "Gabe,
we love you."

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.469
And I'm like --
-It's a team.

00:06:44.469 --> 00:06:45.804
-Yeah, it's a team thing.

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:48.641
It's like on a ship -- and this
is how I think about it.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:52.478
If it's a ship,
like those old Greek ships

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.079
and everybody
has an oar in the water,

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:57.350
like I have my oar
and I'm doing my job.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.819
And as long as I don't screw up,

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.955
the boat's going to get
where it needs to go.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:05.858
But we all have to orient
to the captain's authority.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:08.527
And it's not like --
if you have ego,

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.596
then it's like the ship
doesn't go anywhere

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.664
because it's not my job.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.165
-Well, you make a turn
in the one way

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.800
because you're rowing
too hard on that side.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.669
-You get frustrated because
you're the, you know,

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:18.771
the guy and you take your oar
out of the water

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:20.205
and then it's this
self-fulfilling, like...

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:22.041
-Yeah, and then I see you,
I nudge you, I go,

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.675
"Look, he's not even rowing."

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:24.844
-Yeah, exactly.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.078
And the captain's like,
"What the hell?"

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.613
And you're like, "Well..."

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:28.614
-Talk to Larry.
-Yeah.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.415
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.415 --> 00:07:31.984
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:32.985
Here's...

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.621
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.856
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:39.892
Gabriel Basso.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.628
-Gabriel Basso in
"The Night Agent."

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:44.096
Take a look at this.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:56.475 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:57.943
-Guys, I think
I see a way down.

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.211
Come on.
Take my hand.

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.147
-Okay.
-Come on.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:04.917
-Oh, my God!

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:07.453
-[ Groans, coughs ]

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:09.655
-Are you okay?

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.957
Peter?

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:13.959
-Your turn.
-I'm not jumping down there.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:15.528
-I'll catch you.
-You'll catch me?

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:16.929
-Yes.
-That's crazy.

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.831
-Crazier than waiting around
for your friend? Come on.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:22.468
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.203
-Gabriel Basso.
-What clip was that?

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:28.707
-I quickly wanted to show
what an amazing

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:31.143
artist you are with
pen and ink there.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.478
This is a picture of you.
-Cant' really tell.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.813
-It's a dark photo,
but this -- you --

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:36.047
That looks like Keanu Reeves.

00:08:36.047 --> 00:08:38.050
-Yeah.
-Is it?

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:42.721
-Yeah. He -- he commissioned
a piece for me, and I...

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:43.956
-That is Keanu Reeves.
-Yeah.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.591
-Hey, cool.
-What's funny about

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.927
this picture too,
is like the context of,

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:49.795
Hey, you do pen and ink art
and you can't even see the art.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.263
And it's like, That's Keanu.

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:53.165
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:55.001
Yeah, so...

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:57.236
[ Applause ]

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.603
-Get out of here.

00:08:58.603 --> 00:09:00.606
[ Laughs ]

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.741
Can you come back
on the show Monday?

00:09:02.741 --> 00:09:04.810
I want to keep
talking to you.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.811
You're fascinating.
You'll work it out.

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.146
-You have my number.
-Yeah.

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.214
-Thank you very much.
Gabriel Basso.

00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:12.585
"The Night Agent" is streaming
now on Netflix.

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:14.253
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:15.555
Stick around, everybody.

